1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,480
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,291
Hey! Is anyone there?

3
00:00:27,291 --> 00:00:28,916
Anyone there? Hey!

4
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:32,000
Shut up!

5
00:00:33,583 --> 00:00:35,333
Who are you? Let me out!

6
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:49,958
Who are you? Why am I here? Hey!

7
00:00:50,041 --> 00:00:51,250
It's no use.

8
00:00:54,458 --> 00:00:55,625
And who are you?

9
00:00:57,708 --> 00:00:59,708
I tried before you woke up.

10
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:01,916
They won't open the door.

11
00:01:03,583 --> 00:01:04,583
Why kidnap me?

12
00:01:05,083 --> 00:01:06,333
Why are we at sea?

13
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:08,750
It's over.

14
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:12,166
Jung found out. I'm doomed.

15
00:01:12,958 --> 00:01:15,333
Jung? You mean my boss?

16
00:01:15,416 --> 00:01:16,875
What did he find out?

17
00:01:19,125 --> 00:01:20,833
Do you work for Jung too?

18
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:23,291
I'm his accountant.

19
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:24,833
You got some nerve.

20
00:01:25,375 --> 00:01:27,208
I'm just his driver.

21
00:01:27,291 --> 00:01:28,958
How could I refuse?

22
00:01:29,666 --> 00:01:31,583
What are you talking about?

23
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:36,291
An accountant for a large construction company.

24
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,916
How'd you make time to sleep with his wife?

25
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,541
Sleep with his… How could I possibly do that?

26
00:01:41,625 --> 00:01:43,083
Then why are you here?

27
00:01:45,041 --> 00:01:46,875
Jung can't possibly suspect me.

28
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:49,791
I've only seen his wife twice.

29
00:01:49,875 --> 00:01:51,708
Why explain this to me?

30
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:54,958
You're locked up here, just like me.

31
00:01:56,916 --> 00:01:58,750
Unsure if we'll be tossed into the sea.

32
00:01:59,791 --> 00:02:01,625
He must want to silence me.

33
00:02:02,625 --> 00:02:05,958
He thought I leaked that he was cooking the books.

34
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:09,708
Money laundering?

35
00:02:11,041 --> 00:02:13,416
Jung does that for many politicians and tycoons.

36
00:02:13,916 --> 00:02:15,041
Doesn't everyone know?

37
00:02:15,125 --> 00:02:16,791
Someone must have set me up.

38
00:02:17,291 --> 00:02:19,541
If I'd wanted to rat him out, I would've long ago!

39
00:02:20,416 --> 00:02:23,791
If you left any of that evidence with someone close to you,

40
00:02:23,875 --> 00:02:26,958
perhaps they could expose him after we're dead

41
00:02:27,875 --> 00:02:29,750
in retaliation.

42
00:02:31,125 --> 00:02:34,166
My wife might see the ledgers in my study.

43
00:02:35,166 --> 00:02:37,166
Given who she is, she would never…

44
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:39,041
She wouldn't dare do anything.

45
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:42,500
My son just started junior high school.

46
00:02:43,166 --> 00:02:44,000
I…

47
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,291
The study?

48
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:12,541
You're doing the dirty part next time.

49
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:17,250
Hey, thanks for your cooperation.

50
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:18,250
You tricked me!

51
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:21,416
Someone will make a copy of those ledgers in your study.

52
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,583
That will be me.

53
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:25,375
Don't worry. You and your family will be fine.

54
00:03:25,458 --> 00:03:27,458
There's food and drinks. Help yourself.

55
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:30,333
But if you want to stop us…

56
00:03:30,416 --> 00:03:32,416
Think about how you'll explain it to Jung.

57
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:37,666
My wife might see the ledgers in my study.

58
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:40,541
Given who she is, she would never…

59
00:03:46,416 --> 00:03:48,791
We're on our way to get the ledgers.

60
00:03:48,875 --> 00:03:50,833
No news is good news.

61
00:03:50,916 --> 00:03:52,875
Hurry back after you get them.

62
00:03:52,958 --> 00:03:54,708
Chairman's got a new task for you.

63
00:03:55,208 --> 00:03:57,625
Can we stop working for the police?

64
00:03:57,708 --> 00:03:59,750
It makes us seem like the police.

65
00:04:00,625 --> 00:04:05,000
How could we turn down the head of the National Police Agency?

66
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:08,625
If you have complaints, talk to the chairman.

67
00:04:40,541 --> 00:04:42,583
THE FIXERS

68
00:04:43,833 --> 00:04:47,250
THE SWAMP EEL

69
00:04:48,833 --> 00:04:50,291
Come on.

70
00:04:50,375 --> 00:04:52,208
Get in the zone!

71
00:04:52,291 --> 00:04:55,083
Go big or go home!

72
00:04:55,166 --> 00:04:57,166
Place big bets if you want deep pockets.

73
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:58,375
-Come on! -Okay.

74
00:04:58,458 --> 00:04:59,625
Here.

75
00:04:59,708 --> 00:05:00,750
No more bets.

76
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:01,791
Big!

77
00:05:01,875 --> 00:05:04,625
-Small. -Big.

78
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,333
Come on!

79
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:08,708
Here it goes!

80
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:10,958
Triple takes it all.

81
00:05:11,041 --> 00:05:13,958
The triple takes it all. Say "uncle," you all.

82
00:05:14,041 --> 00:05:15,833
Okay. Quit gambling today.

83
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:17,958
What are you doing here? Continue.

84
00:05:18,041 --> 00:05:19,416
Want to leave after winning?

85
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,041
Sorry. Got dinner with my pretty wife.

86
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:23,166
Who are you kidding?

87
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,000
Yours is waiting for you too, damn it.

88
00:05:25,083 --> 00:05:26,625
I have no wife today. Continue.

89
00:05:26,708 --> 00:05:30,208
Continue.

90
00:05:30,708 --> 00:05:31,666
Wait, hold on.

91
00:05:32,166 --> 00:05:33,000
Goddamn it.

92
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:34,291
What? Running off on us?

93
00:05:35,541 --> 00:05:37,666
Do not go gentle into that good night.

94
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:40,125
Everything will turn out right. Hurry.

95
00:05:42,041 --> 00:05:43,583
Hey, Milky.

96
00:05:43,666 --> 00:05:45,000
What the heck?

97
00:05:45,083 --> 00:05:46,625
Oh, Pond Loach.

98
00:05:46,708 --> 00:05:47,625
My goodness.

99
00:05:48,625 --> 00:05:50,375
-Business is good. -Milky.

100
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:52,500
I'm Swamp Eel.

101
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:56,583
-I'll make it for you. -Make, my ass.

102
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:59,125
You're two months late on your protection money.

103
00:05:59,208 --> 00:06:00,416
Well, Milky…

104
00:06:01,458 --> 00:06:04,333
Business hasn't been great lately.

105
00:06:06,083 --> 00:06:06,916
How about this?

106
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,541
Let's go another round?

107
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:10,750
Yeah, let's go again!

108
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,041
Come on.

109
00:06:18,458 --> 00:06:19,291
That much?

110
00:06:19,375 --> 00:06:21,625
-All in? -All in on big.

111
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:26,375
Bet on big!

112
00:06:26,875 --> 00:06:28,583
Okay, no more bets.

113
00:06:28,666 --> 00:06:30,750
No regrets.

114
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:39,708
Big!

115
00:06:39,791 --> 00:06:41,208
Show it!

116
00:06:41,291 --> 00:06:43,125
Big!

117
00:06:43,208 --> 00:06:44,375
Show it.

118
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:46,125
What's up? Too scared to reveal it?

119
00:06:47,791 --> 00:06:48,875
Who's afraid?

120
00:06:49,375 --> 00:06:51,291
Here it goes!

121
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:53,916
Fuck you! Cheater!

122
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,416
No.

123
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:57,166
Milky, listen to me.

124
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:59,708
Maybe the fan was too strong. It shifted the dice.

125
00:06:59,791 --> 00:07:00,916
I didn't cheat.

126
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,916
Keep spouting nonsense.

127
00:07:04,083 --> 00:07:06,666
I know your greatest asset

128
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:09,541
is this golden index finger.

129
00:07:10,208 --> 00:07:13,291
Your former boss got a 30-million-dollar policy on it.

130
00:07:13,875 --> 00:07:15,416
You see what I'm saying now?

131
00:07:17,541 --> 00:07:18,500
Fine.

132
00:07:18,583 --> 00:07:19,916
I'll pay.

133
00:07:21,375 --> 00:07:22,208
Move.

134
00:07:22,291 --> 00:07:23,166
Move aside.

135
00:07:27,666 --> 00:07:29,333
Pay, your ass!

136
00:07:30,666 --> 00:07:31,500
Chase him!

137
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Granny, gotta go!

138
00:07:34,083 --> 00:07:35,250
-Collectors again? -No!

139
00:07:40,625 --> 00:07:41,916
Stop!

140
00:07:44,458 --> 00:07:45,416
-You're fine. -Stop!

141
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,500
Help me!

142
00:07:48,833 --> 00:07:50,375
Fuck. Let's go.

143
00:08:00,958 --> 00:08:02,625
Where is he? Fuck!

144
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:12,791
Fuck you. Stop!

145
00:08:13,375 --> 00:08:14,416
Stop!

146
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:18,791
Come on.

147
00:08:19,875 --> 00:08:20,875
Shit, he's climbing!

148
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,541
-This monkey! -Damn it!

149
00:08:29,625 --> 00:08:30,583
Fuck.

150
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:35,458
Fuck! Still running?

151
00:08:45,875 --> 00:08:47,958
-Hello? -Dad, we're screwed.

152
00:08:48,041 --> 00:08:49,458
I know that.

153
00:08:49,541 --> 00:08:50,458
I don't mean you.

154
00:08:50,541 --> 00:08:51,708
It's Mom.

155
00:08:51,791 --> 00:08:53,833
Over there.

156
00:08:59,458 --> 00:09:00,750
You fucking traitor.

157
00:09:00,833 --> 00:09:02,708
-Stop! -Stop! Fuck!

158
00:09:04,416 --> 00:09:05,250
Fuck! Stop!

159
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:07,958
Fuck, you damn old ape! Motherfucker!

160
00:09:09,875 --> 00:09:10,791
Stop!

161
00:09:11,541 --> 00:09:14,208
-What's with the chase? -Don't let me catch you!

162
00:09:18,083 --> 00:09:19,000
Need this!

163
00:09:33,583 --> 00:09:35,000
Hey, my swamp eel!

164
00:09:42,125 --> 00:09:43,041
Motherfucker.

165
00:09:43,125 --> 00:09:44,000
Fuck!

166
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:56,041
So many of you? Not down there!

167
00:09:58,958 --> 00:10:00,000
Fuck you!

168
00:10:01,958 --> 00:10:02,791
Get out!

169
00:10:08,458 --> 00:10:10,000
Stop, motherfucker!

170
00:10:10,625 --> 00:10:12,250
Stop fighting!

171
00:10:20,333 --> 00:10:21,375
Beat him!

172
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:26,208
Move it!

173
00:10:28,833 --> 00:10:29,708
Come on!

174
00:10:29,791 --> 00:10:31,083
Come on!

175
00:10:32,291 --> 00:10:33,583
Come on!

176
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,041
Fuck! Chase!

177
00:10:40,625 --> 00:10:42,208
Tell us if there's a problem.

178
00:10:42,291 --> 00:10:43,166
Bye.

179
00:10:43,916 --> 00:10:46,208
Hey! Officer.

180
00:10:46,791 --> 00:10:48,541
-Are you okay? -Can I get a ride home?

181
00:10:49,125 --> 00:10:51,458
-What's wrong? -So I have diabetes.

182
00:10:51,541 --> 00:10:54,833
I left my insulin syringe at home.

183
00:10:54,916 --> 00:10:56,083
So, yes?

184
00:10:56,166 --> 00:10:57,208
You need an ambulance?

185
00:10:57,291 --> 00:10:58,750
No. It's faster if you drive me.

186
00:10:58,833 --> 00:11:00,416
Okay. Come on. Watch out.

187
00:11:02,333 --> 00:11:04,791
Ask him for his address. We'll take him home.

188
00:11:05,291 --> 00:11:06,125
Come on.

189
00:11:07,916 --> 00:11:12,750
I am the captain of my soul. The police protect the people.

190
00:11:12,833 --> 00:11:14,500
Bud, what's going on? Where's your mom?

191
00:11:14,583 --> 00:11:15,750
Live streaming.

192
00:11:15,833 --> 00:11:18,375
-Why? Isn't she in trouble? -See for yourself.

193
00:11:21,708 --> 00:11:24,875
He told me to buy some kind of cryptocurrency.

194
00:11:24,958 --> 00:11:26,208
It went up over 100 times.

195
00:11:26,291 --> 00:11:28,208
Over 100 times!

196
00:11:28,291 --> 00:11:31,375
He said the company was launching a new coin

197
00:11:31,458 --> 00:11:33,375
that would surge and was a must-buy.

198
00:11:33,458 --> 00:11:35,458
So I bought it. Look.

199
00:11:36,375 --> 00:11:37,458
In just half a month…

200
00:11:38,041 --> 00:11:40,291
-12%. It went up 12%! -Seriously?

201
00:11:40,375 --> 00:11:41,583
My husband often says,

202
00:11:41,666 --> 00:11:43,916
"Press your wins and go for broke."

203
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,166
-So I had to buy more, right? -Do I?

204
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,750
-I guess? -Do I?

205
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:49,833
Hey, own what you said, all right?

206
00:11:49,916 --> 00:11:52,708
I wanted to cash out. But guess what?

207
00:11:52,791 --> 00:11:55,583
The company said it was under investigation. Look.

208
00:11:55,666 --> 00:11:57,833
I can't get any of my money back!

209
00:11:58,458 --> 00:12:00,625
It's fine. It's just five million.

210
00:12:01,916 --> 00:12:03,375
Shipping next month. Promise.

211
00:12:03,458 --> 00:12:05,625
Delivered fresh to your door.

212
00:12:05,708 --> 00:12:08,666
Gosh, when has Wonder Wendy ever lied to you?

213
00:12:08,750 --> 00:12:10,833
Didn't you say it was an investment?

214
00:12:10,916 --> 00:12:13,083
-Report it to the police. -I already did.

215
00:12:13,166 --> 00:12:15,875
They said I might never get it back.

216
00:12:15,958 --> 00:12:17,083
Hold up.

217
00:12:17,166 --> 00:12:18,666
I'm a victim.

218
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:20,708
You should be comforting, not scolding me.

219
00:12:20,791 --> 00:12:23,000
I don't mind that you play mah-jongg all day.

220
00:12:23,083 --> 00:12:25,083
But you got scammed. Why wouldn't I scold you?

221
00:12:25,166 --> 00:12:26,458
I should be the one talking.

222
00:12:26,541 --> 00:12:29,166
You go out every day and come home all dirty.

223
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:30,500
You might have a mistress.

224
00:12:33,666 --> 00:12:35,541
I say you're obsessed with money.

225
00:12:35,625 --> 00:12:37,125
Scammers love people like you.

226
00:12:37,208 --> 00:12:38,333
Felix Chiang.

227
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:41,083
Be honest with yourself.

228
00:12:41,166 --> 00:12:43,083
In all the time we've been married,

229
00:12:43,166 --> 00:12:44,916
have I ever had an easy day?

230
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,916
Still, I raised our child and helped bring in extra money.

231
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,416
This family would've collapsed otherwise.

232
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:53,083
So now it's my problem?

233
00:12:53,166 --> 00:12:55,541
-My fault? -No.

234
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:56,833
I…

235
00:12:56,916 --> 00:12:59,541
I just want to earn a little more money.

236
00:12:59,625 --> 00:13:00,625
All right.

237
00:13:00,708 --> 00:13:02,000
We can earn that money back.

238
00:13:02,083 --> 00:13:03,416
I'll take care of it.

239
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:04,333
Hey.

240
00:13:04,416 --> 00:13:06,333
That was a lot. How will you manage?

241
00:13:06,416 --> 00:13:08,250
Please, who do you think I am?

242
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:11,916
This amount used to be nothing to me, okay?

243
00:13:13,166 --> 00:13:15,541
By the way, where's the money from?

244
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,375
I just…

245
00:13:20,458 --> 00:13:24,000
used our house as collateral and borrowed that in your name.

246
00:13:27,625 --> 00:13:29,166
You're so smart.

247
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:31,125
You're incredible!

248
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:50,000
CHIU CHA TEMPLE

249
00:14:11,791 --> 00:14:12,833
Ma'am.

250
00:14:13,625 --> 00:14:15,000
Are you seeking guidance?

251
00:14:22,583 --> 00:14:24,208
CONSULTATION FORM, CHAO MING-CHENG

252
00:14:24,291 --> 00:14:26,041
Please draw a fortune stick.

253
00:14:26,125 --> 00:14:27,500
No need for divination blocks.

254
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,333
FANG CHIAO-HUI

255
00:14:40,208 --> 00:14:41,916
The fortune slip reads,

256
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,166
"Let he who tied the bell on the tiger take it off."

257
00:14:47,041 --> 00:14:49,833
If Mr. Chao runs into any trouble,

258
00:14:49,916 --> 00:14:52,083
tell him to handle it himself.

259
00:14:54,291 --> 00:14:55,291
How did it go?

260
00:14:55,791 --> 00:14:57,708
They want you to go there in person.

261
00:15:23,166 --> 00:15:27,000
CHING HE TEMPLE

262
00:15:42,958 --> 00:15:44,125
This way, please.

263
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:54,458
CHAO MING-CHENG

264
00:15:58,750 --> 00:15:59,958
Mr. Chao.

265
00:16:01,666 --> 00:16:03,166
Are you in trouble?

266
00:16:07,583 --> 00:16:08,875
Please come with me.

267
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:44,916
TAI SUI HALL

268
00:16:46,541 --> 00:16:49,125
I am Thackery Huang, the chairman of Ching He.

269
00:16:49,625 --> 00:16:53,333
What can I do for you, Mr. Chao?

270
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:58,958
As Attorney Chao Ming-cheng is seeking reelection to the legislature,

271
00:16:59,041 --> 00:17:01,375
news broke of his son's drug possession.

272
00:17:01,875 --> 00:17:02,791
The leaked video…

273
00:17:02,875 --> 00:17:04,708
MING-CHENG'S SON PASSED OUT WITH SUSPECTED DRUGS

274
00:17:04,791 --> 00:17:06,625
What do you think of this?

275
00:17:06,708 --> 00:17:10,916
Party leaders will likely shift their support to Lu Shu-jung

276
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,416
and force Chao to withdraw.

277
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,500
Then I shall congratulate you.

278
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:18,166
Lu Shu-jung is a conservative within the party.

279
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:21,541
If she is elected, it will help you become mayor.

280
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:24,291
-It's the minister. -Hello, sir.

281
00:17:24,375 --> 00:17:25,583
MING YOUNG PARTY FUNDRAISER

282
00:17:25,666 --> 00:17:28,416
Sir, many note that you are still active in retirement.

283
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,208
If your eldest son becomes mayor,

284
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:32,291
will he be a puppet mayor?

285
00:17:32,791 --> 00:17:33,958
What's your response?

286
00:17:34,041 --> 00:17:36,375
Let's keep the focus on today's fundraiser.

287
00:17:36,458 --> 00:17:38,208
Sir, please wait and take a photo.

288
00:17:46,375 --> 00:17:47,625
Louis.

289
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,333
Join us.

290
00:17:49,833 --> 00:17:52,125
-Come. -Who is this young man?

291
00:17:54,083 --> 00:17:56,791
-The second son of the Hsuehs? -No, that's impossible.

292
00:17:56,875 --> 00:17:59,166
Doesn't he have only one son? I've never seen him before.

293
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:00,416
Stand in the middle.

294
00:18:19,458 --> 00:18:20,583
Yung?

295
00:18:21,458 --> 00:18:23,041
-What's up? -Just warning you.

296
00:18:23,125 --> 00:18:26,458
Milky is telling people that you rig your games.

297
00:18:26,958 --> 00:18:30,250
I heard your family got scammed for five million dollars.

298
00:18:30,333 --> 00:18:31,291
How did you know?

299
00:18:31,375 --> 00:18:33,875
Didn't your wife cry in front of the world?

300
00:18:34,708 --> 00:18:37,708
The news is all over. What are your plans now?

301
00:18:37,791 --> 00:18:41,333
If that venue is no good anymore, I'll go somewhere else.

302
00:18:41,416 --> 00:18:44,125
I'll pay off the debts before I die

303
00:18:44,208 --> 00:18:46,416
and make a little more for my wife and son.

304
00:18:46,916 --> 00:18:48,750
I have a gig that pays quick cash.

305
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:50,291
Someone owes my friend money.

306
00:18:50,375 --> 00:18:53,625
You just have to flash a gun as a warning.

307
00:18:53,708 --> 00:18:55,500
I don't touch guns anymore.

308
00:18:55,583 --> 00:18:57,458
You were such a badass. If you return--

309
00:18:57,541 --> 00:19:00,625
I wandered lonely as a cloud. Cut the crap and spit it out.

310
00:19:00,708 --> 00:19:03,041
That was so long ago, all right?

311
00:19:03,125 --> 00:19:05,666
I called you 'cause I knew you wouldn't pull the trigger.

312
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:09,166
300,000 dollars. No need to shoot. Just flash a gun.

313
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,125
Well?

314
00:19:10,875 --> 00:19:14,250
Didn't I tell you already? I don't touch guns anymore.

315
00:19:14,833 --> 00:19:16,875
Think about it. I'll call you again.

316
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:18,291
Find someone else.

317
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:36,666
Dad, what are you looking for?

318
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:38,291
You scared me to death.

319
00:19:38,375 --> 00:19:42,250
Have you seen a tin box with a floral pattern?

320
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:44,333
No. Why are you looking for that?

321
00:19:47,333 --> 00:19:49,000
Hey, listen.

322
00:19:49,083 --> 00:19:51,625
Earn big and support your mom. Okay? Don't be like me.

323
00:19:52,125 --> 00:19:56,083
Don't underestimate her. She'll earn it all back by live streaming.

324
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:57,291
How was she?

325
00:19:57,791 --> 00:19:59,333
She was on the phone with Auntie.

326
00:19:59,416 --> 00:20:02,125
"Gosh, how could I be so stupid and sell the house?"

327
00:20:02,208 --> 00:20:03,750
Nothing you haven't heard before.

328
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,083
Found it.

329
00:20:13,666 --> 00:20:15,666
-What's inside? -Nothing.

330
00:20:16,166 --> 00:20:17,833
Aren't midterms tomorrow? Go study.

331
00:20:17,916 --> 00:20:18,750
Okay.

332
00:20:20,375 --> 00:20:21,208
Bud.

333
00:20:23,375 --> 00:20:24,666
Good luck.

334
00:20:25,416 --> 00:20:27,000
Don't worry, bud.

335
00:20:31,833 --> 00:20:33,083
-Hello? -Hello?

336
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:34,958
So?

337
00:20:35,666 --> 00:20:38,375
Stop overthinking. It's decided.

338
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,541
I'll send you the address.

339
00:20:54,708 --> 00:20:56,666
Goddamn it.

340
00:21:16,666 --> 00:21:18,166
Mr. Hung, long time no see.

341
00:21:18,250 --> 00:21:19,541
Long time no see.

342
00:21:20,041 --> 00:21:21,500
This is Tristan, my son.

343
00:21:21,583 --> 00:21:23,625
Here. This is Minister Wang.

344
00:21:23,708 --> 00:21:24,833
This is Minister Chen.

345
00:21:25,333 --> 00:21:27,291
-Hello. -Nice to meet you.

346
00:21:27,375 --> 00:21:30,416
Please look after this young man.

347
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:31,416
He's promising.

348
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:40,291
-Hey, hello. -Hello.

349
00:21:40,375 --> 00:21:44,125
-Sir, long time no see. -I should call you Legislator Lu now.

350
00:21:44,208 --> 00:21:45,291
Oh, no.

351
00:21:45,375 --> 00:21:49,875
But the decision on this seat could indeed come early tonight.

352
00:21:49,958 --> 00:21:54,333
I'm sure you have many plans for when you become a legislator.

353
00:21:54,416 --> 00:21:55,750
Don't worry.

354
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:59,666
I will personally oversee the Hsin Nan redevelopment project.

355
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:00,875
It will all go smoothly.

356
00:22:04,041 --> 00:22:05,666
One vodka martini.

357
00:22:06,833 --> 00:22:08,250
Make it a double.

358
00:22:09,458 --> 00:22:11,166
I don't need to be sober for this.

359
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:15,291
What's your drink?

360
00:22:16,708 --> 00:22:17,750
Orange juice.

361
00:22:19,208 --> 00:22:21,125
You don't need alcohol for such an event?

362
00:22:21,958 --> 00:22:23,875
I can't drink. I'm working.

363
00:22:24,791 --> 00:22:25,625
Make it two.

364
00:22:27,125 --> 00:22:28,583
All the more reason to drink.

365
00:22:29,083 --> 00:22:30,916
Louis Hsueh. Hello.

366
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,541
Are you Mr. Hsueh's son?

367
00:22:34,250 --> 00:22:36,500
Hello. I'm Viki, Lu Shu-jung's aide.

368
00:22:36,583 --> 00:22:38,833
I haven't seen you much at events like this.

369
00:22:38,916 --> 00:22:41,333
My dad rarely brings me to these occasions.

370
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:42,833
I'm not a socializer.

371
00:22:42,916 --> 00:22:44,041
I get it.

372
00:22:49,625 --> 00:22:50,833
Sorry.

373
00:22:50,916 --> 00:22:52,583
-Sorry. Your pants. -It's okay.

374
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,250
How will you compensate me?

375
00:23:08,375 --> 00:23:10,291
Why don't we exchange our numbers?

376
00:23:22,666 --> 00:23:23,833
Excuse me.

377
00:23:23,916 --> 00:23:25,708
I didn't expect you to be so bold.

378
00:23:25,791 --> 00:23:27,291
There are many people downstairs.

379
00:23:27,375 --> 00:23:28,833
You've done this before.

380
00:23:31,291 --> 00:23:32,375
What do you mean?

381
00:23:32,458 --> 00:23:34,666
I can't believe a PhD graduate

382
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,791
had to hook up with her boss's husband

383
00:23:38,541 --> 00:23:40,291
to become an assistant.

384
00:23:40,375 --> 00:23:41,875
Where did you get that photo?

385
00:23:42,458 --> 00:23:43,875
I'm the one asking now.

386
00:23:44,958 --> 00:23:46,333
What do you want?

387
00:23:46,833 --> 00:23:48,458
Chao Ming-cheng's son's drug case.

388
00:23:48,541 --> 00:23:50,125
Did you hire someone to frame him?

389
00:23:52,166 --> 00:23:53,791
I don't know what you're saying.

390
00:23:56,375 --> 00:23:58,916
Do you think I should post these photos online

391
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,916
or send them to the press downstairs?

392
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:04,583
Are you backing me into a corner?

393
00:24:05,083 --> 00:24:06,458
I don't have to post them.

394
00:24:07,166 --> 00:24:09,500
I only want to know who you hired.

395
00:24:18,708 --> 00:24:20,875
Lu Shu-jung's husband hired Noods.

396
00:24:23,541 --> 00:24:25,041
In exchange for what?

397
00:24:25,583 --> 00:24:27,666
When Lu Shu-jung becomes a legislator,

398
00:24:28,166 --> 00:24:30,208
his business won't be investigated.

399
00:24:30,291 --> 00:24:31,958
Is Lu Shu-jung that resourceful?

400
00:24:33,333 --> 00:24:34,583
Of course not.

401
00:24:35,291 --> 00:24:36,625
When she succeeds,

402
00:24:36,708 --> 00:24:40,041
I'll pay someone to anonymously report him for drug dealing and kidnapping.

403
00:24:40,125 --> 00:24:42,375
She just has to deny everything.

404
00:24:46,750 --> 00:24:48,083
When she succeeds,

405
00:24:48,166 --> 00:24:51,375
I'll pay someone to anonymously report him for drug dealing and kidnapping.

406
00:24:52,541 --> 00:24:55,458
If you don't tell anyone what happened here,

407
00:24:55,541 --> 00:24:58,125
you and these photos will remain safe.

408
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:04,250
As Attorney Chao Ming-cheng is seeking reelection to the legislature,

409
00:25:04,333 --> 00:25:06,750
news broke that his son was in possession of drugs.

410
00:25:06,833 --> 00:25:10,750
The leaked video clearly shows unidentified powder around him.

411
00:25:10,833 --> 00:25:13,583
Chao, who spoke of the rule of law and clean governance--

412
00:25:14,083 --> 00:25:14,916
Hey.

413
00:25:15,416 --> 00:25:16,250
Are you going in?

414
00:25:16,333 --> 00:25:18,000
How come it's a pig farm?

415
00:25:18,541 --> 00:25:21,250
It's a cover for Noods's business that packages drugs.

416
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:23,750
Something feels wrong.

417
00:25:24,250 --> 00:25:29,000
What? Have you lost your guts after being away for so long?

418
00:25:29,083 --> 00:25:31,250
Don't worry. Nobody knows you're there.

419
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:32,666
All right.

420
00:25:42,458 --> 00:25:43,666
Noods.

421
00:25:44,166 --> 00:25:46,208
Is it worth risking your life for them?

422
00:25:46,708 --> 00:25:49,416
Hey, how much did they pay you?

423
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:52,166
Don't know what you mean. Shoot me if you dare.

424
00:25:52,250 --> 00:25:54,000
It's not about the money.

425
00:25:56,083 --> 00:25:57,458
Won't talk, huh?

426
00:25:59,125 --> 00:26:00,375
Of course not.

427
00:26:00,875 --> 00:26:02,250
When she succeeds,

428
00:26:02,333 --> 00:26:05,541
I'll pay someone to anonymously report him for drug dealing and kidnapping.

429
00:26:05,625 --> 00:26:07,833
She just has to deny everything.

430
00:26:09,333 --> 00:26:12,083
They used you. Now they're throwing you under the bus.

431
00:26:12,166 --> 00:26:15,041
Fuck, you can't trust a politician's word.

432
00:26:15,125 --> 00:26:16,083
What do you want?

433
00:26:16,583 --> 00:26:19,625
Give me the evidence that Mr. Chao's son was framed,

434
00:26:19,708 --> 00:26:22,375
and I guarantee you'll get out of this safe and sound.

435
00:26:23,750 --> 00:26:25,625
You'll get paid too.

436
00:26:31,916 --> 00:26:33,291
It's in the pigsty outside.

437
00:28:41,875 --> 00:28:42,708
Buddy.

438
00:28:43,541 --> 00:28:44,875
I didn't mean to shoot you.

439
00:28:45,833 --> 00:28:48,125
I really didn't see anything.

440
00:28:50,375 --> 00:28:52,000
You don't work for Noods?

441
00:28:52,083 --> 00:28:53,083
No.

442
00:28:53,166 --> 00:28:55,208
I was sent here to collect a debt from him.

443
00:29:12,666 --> 00:29:15,000
Bring me the bag over there.

444
00:29:28,375 --> 00:29:30,458
GOLD

445
00:29:30,958 --> 00:29:32,416
-Hello? -Did you get it?

446
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,041
I got shot.

447
00:29:34,125 --> 00:29:35,666
Where are you? I'm coming.

448
00:29:35,750 --> 00:29:37,041
No need.

449
00:29:37,583 --> 00:29:38,750
There's no time.

450
00:29:39,500 --> 00:29:42,000
I'll send the file to you first. Hold on.

451
00:29:47,791 --> 00:29:49,625
Motherfucker.

452
00:29:50,916 --> 00:29:54,541
I got the video, but the phone is broken. I can't send it to you.

453
00:29:55,291 --> 00:29:56,666
Someone's with you?

454
00:30:08,708 --> 00:30:09,541
Hello?

455
00:30:09,625 --> 00:30:12,541
The client goes on stage in 30 minutes.

456
00:30:13,125 --> 00:30:14,833
Have you found the evidence yet?

457
00:30:14,916 --> 00:30:17,166
Look someone up for me. I'll send you a photo.

458
00:30:22,333 --> 00:30:25,791
FELIX CHIANG, SWAMP EEL, 55 YEARS OLD

459
00:30:25,875 --> 00:30:27,333
Put me on speaker.

460
00:30:29,916 --> 00:30:31,333
Felix Chiang.

461
00:30:31,833 --> 00:30:32,750
Who are you?

462
00:30:32,833 --> 00:30:36,708
Bring the phone in 20 minutes. Kuang He Road Garage, top floor.

463
00:30:36,791 --> 00:30:38,958
Hand it over to a red sports car.

464
00:30:39,041 --> 00:30:41,291
Why should I do this for you?

465
00:30:42,083 --> 00:30:43,500
Howie Chiang.

466
00:30:43,583 --> 00:30:45,041
Your son's got a nice name.

467
00:30:45,125 --> 00:30:46,750
Attends Ping Cheng Junior High.

468
00:30:46,833 --> 00:30:48,333
Top 30 at school.

469
00:30:48,416 --> 00:30:49,250
How did you know?

470
00:30:49,958 --> 00:30:51,041
What do you want?

471
00:30:51,541 --> 00:30:52,500
Twenty minutes.

472
00:30:52,583 --> 00:30:54,750
Bring the phone in 20 minutes.

473
00:30:55,416 --> 00:30:58,000
You and your family will be safe.

474
00:30:58,500 --> 00:31:01,041
Otherwise, you'll find out.

475
00:31:01,625 --> 00:31:03,333
-Motherfucker. -Thank you.

476
00:31:07,041 --> 00:31:08,333
Damn it.

477
00:31:08,875 --> 00:31:11,875
Hey, is that your car? Quick.

478
00:31:31,125 --> 00:31:32,208
Mr. Chao.

479
00:31:32,708 --> 00:31:35,541
You'll be on stage in ten minutes. Are you ready?

480
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,166
Don't be so cocky.

481
00:31:40,125 --> 00:31:42,583
I'll settle the score with you one day.

482
00:31:42,666 --> 00:31:44,250
Sure. I'll wait.

483
00:31:44,333 --> 00:31:46,125
Sir, it's time to get ready.

484
00:31:46,208 --> 00:31:48,458
The host will go over the rundown.

485
00:31:53,583 --> 00:31:55,333
-I can't reach Noods. -How can that be?

486
00:31:55,416 --> 00:31:56,916
GPS shows it's nearing the venue.

487
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,333
Take care of this no matter what.

488
00:32:13,833 --> 00:32:16,708
BREAD AND CAKES

489
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:31,875
Hurry up.

490
00:32:34,750 --> 00:32:36,250
Did you come from the pigsty?

491
00:32:36,333 --> 00:32:37,750
Isn't that obvious?

492
00:32:37,833 --> 00:32:39,666
-Stand back and wait. -Hold up.

493
00:32:39,750 --> 00:32:41,583
I delivered it. Can I go now?

494
00:32:41,666 --> 00:32:43,458
Wait. Let me check it first.

495
00:32:54,041 --> 00:32:55,500
Hurry up.

496
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:08,416
Bring the phone to Chao Ming-cheng at the fundraiser next door.

497
00:33:08,500 --> 00:33:10,625
Why should I? Deliver it yourself.

498
00:33:10,708 --> 00:33:12,166
Ridiculous.

499
00:33:12,250 --> 00:33:14,333
Top 30 at school.

500
00:33:14,958 --> 00:33:17,375
What a pity it would be to lose him.

501
00:33:36,208 --> 00:33:37,250
It's him. Get him!

502
00:33:40,208 --> 00:33:42,333
Bastard! Stop!

503
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:44,833
Come back!

504
00:33:45,500 --> 00:33:47,250
-Fuck! -Come back!

505
00:33:47,958 --> 00:33:48,916
Stop!

506
00:33:49,416 --> 00:33:50,500
Stop!

507
00:33:51,916 --> 00:33:53,500
If you stop, I stop!

508
00:33:53,583 --> 00:33:54,625
-Stop! -Fuck!

509
00:33:54,708 --> 00:33:56,708
MING YOUNG PARTY

510
00:34:03,666 --> 00:34:04,666
Hello, everyone.

511
00:34:05,375 --> 00:34:06,666
I am Chao Ming-cheng.

512
00:34:07,875 --> 00:34:10,666
Thank you for all your support.

513
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:13,125
Since entering politics,

514
00:34:14,125 --> 00:34:17,541
I've worked diligently every day to serve the people.

515
00:34:18,041 --> 00:34:21,541
I have never done anything against my conscience.

516
00:34:23,916 --> 00:34:26,958
However, now that I'm older,

517
00:34:27,541 --> 00:34:28,916
my mind has changed.

518
00:34:30,458 --> 00:34:32,500
All right. Enough.

519
00:34:32,583 --> 00:34:34,708
Where's the stuff for Chao Ming-cheng?

520
00:34:37,500 --> 00:34:39,250
Didn't I already tell you?

521
00:34:39,333 --> 00:34:40,750
It's in the phone.

522
00:34:40,833 --> 00:34:41,916
Are you playing dumb?

523
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:43,416
There are only porn videos.

524
00:34:44,875 --> 00:34:45,750
Fuck.

525
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:47,958
He likes watching porn that much?

526
00:34:48,041 --> 00:34:49,125
How would I know?

527
00:34:49,208 --> 00:34:51,458
Damn, still playing dumb with me? Beat him up!

528
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:02,541
CHING HE TEMPLE

529
00:35:03,416 --> 00:35:05,125
Such a good runner.

530
00:35:06,166 --> 00:35:07,250
Fuck.

531
00:35:08,458 --> 00:35:09,750
Run again.

532
00:35:14,500 --> 00:35:15,583
Over the years,

533
00:35:16,583 --> 00:35:18,541
I have devoted all my time to work…

534
00:35:20,750 --> 00:35:22,416
and neglected my family.

535
00:35:23,666 --> 00:35:25,291
After careful consideration,

536
00:35:26,416 --> 00:35:28,541
-I formally announce-- -Sir.

537
00:35:41,541 --> 00:35:42,791
I formally announce

538
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,458
that I won't quit the race.

539
00:35:46,625 --> 00:35:50,000
I have proof that my son was falsely accused!

540
00:35:51,041 --> 00:35:53,250
These rumors won't defeat me!

541
00:35:53,333 --> 00:35:54,958
I'll continue to serve the people.

542
00:35:55,750 --> 00:35:56,625
I won't back down!

543
00:36:02,166 --> 00:36:05,500
This isn't convincing. Sprinkle more. Get some powder on him.

544
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:11,458
MISSION COMPLETE

545
00:36:22,666 --> 00:36:23,750
Get out!

546
00:36:23,833 --> 00:36:25,708
You tricked me! Get out!

547
00:36:27,625 --> 00:36:29,041
How did you escape that?

548
00:36:29,125 --> 00:36:32,000
Fuck! I used to take on over a dozen men.

549
00:36:32,083 --> 00:36:33,000
They're nothing!

550
00:36:33,083 --> 00:36:34,833
